### An Open Resource for Fashion Designers, Boutique Owners and Textile Enthusiasts

Choosing the right fabric is one of the most important decisions in garment design.

A fabric's texture, weight, drape, weave and finishing determine how a finished garment looks, feels and performs.

This repository is a practical reference for anyone exploring textile sourcing, fabric selection, and material suitability for fashion projects.

It covers common fabric categories, sourcing considerations, quality checks, and useful resources for buyers.

---

## 1. Understanding Common Fabric Types

Different fabrics serve different purposes depending on their structure, fibre composition, and finishing.

| Fabric | Characteristics | Common Applications |
|---|---|---|
| Georgette | Lightweight, textured, flowing | Sarees, dresses, anarkalis |
| Organza | Crisp, sheer, structured | Dupattas, overlays, statement sleeves |
| Velvet | Soft pile, rich appearance | Jackets, blouses, winter occasion wear |
| Net | Open construction, often sheer | Lehenga overlays, embroidered gowns |
| Crepe | Textured surface, variable drape | Dresses, tops, co-ord sets |
| Banarasi Brocade | Decorative woven patterns | Traditional jackets, lehengas, blouses |
| Cotton | Breathable, versatile | Shirts, kurtas, everyday clothing |
| Silk | Natural fibre with varied textures | Sarees, formalwear, occasion wear |

**Note:** Fabric properties vary depending on fibre composition, weight, weave, and finishing.

