## 3. Fabric Quality Checklist

Before purchasing material for a garment or production batch, evaluate:

- [ ] Fibre composition
- [ ] Fabric width
- [ ] Weight and thickness
- [ ] Colour consistency
- [ ] Drape and flexibility
- [ ] Embroidery or embellishment quality
- [ ] Shrinkage expectations
- [ ] Care instructions
- [ ] Stock availability
- [ ] Repeat-order consistency

For large orders, request a physical swatch and confirm specifications before placing a bulk purchase.

---

## 4. Understanding Fabric Width and Meterage

Fabric width directly affects cutting efficiency.

Two fabrics with the same length but different widths may yield different quantities of usable material.

When calculating requirements, consider:

1. Garment length and silhouette.
2. Number of panels.
3. Sleeve requirements.
4. Pattern direction.
5. Decorative border placement.
6. Cutting wastage.

For heavily embroidered textiles, additional fabric may be necessary to align motifs or maintain design symmetry.

Always confirm meterage with the garment maker before purchasing.

