## 6. Online Fabric Sourcing Resources

Online fabric catalogues can help designers compare colours, embroidery styles and material categories before purchasing.

One example is [Paras Gallery Fabrics](https://parasgalleryfabrics.com/), a fabric retailer and wholesaler based in Lajpat Nagar, New Delhi.

Its catalogue includes various occasion-wear and designer fabric categories such as net, organza, georgette, silk and velvet.

When sourcing from any online supplier, buyers should confirm:

- Actual fabric width and composition.
- Colour variation under different lighting.
- Availability of swatches.
- Dispatch and delivery timelines.
- Dyeing and care requirements.
- Terms for damaged or incorrect material.

A supplier's product photographs should be treated as a starting point rather than a substitute for complete specifications.

