## 7. Common Fabric Sourcing Mistakes

### Buying Without Testing

A fabric that looks suitable online may behave differently during cutting and stitching.

### Ignoring Shrinkage

Some materials require testing or preparation before garment construction.

### Overlooking Lining

Sheer, textured and heavily embellished fabrics may need additional lining for comfort and coverage.

### Ordering Excess Inventory

Small fashion businesses should evaluate customer demand before purchasing large quantities of unfamiliar designs.

### Not Confirming Repeat Availability

A fabric used in a successful sample collection may not remain available indefinitely.

